{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GKFwhipoC47L1unRGW4iCi","type":"tool_result","content":"55:- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n219:## 3. Views (projections)\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n222:- `E.VIEW_ORDER: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side`: the order game.nextView() cycles through when a game doesn't set game.views ('overhead' is left out)\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n228:- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\n244:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n486:- `game.nextView(dir = 1)`: cycle through game.views (or every view): bind it to a key for players who like to switch\n488:- `game.onView(f)` †: call f(view) whenever the view changes (re-bake caches, move HUD)\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n494:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n515:- `game.baseView` †: the chosen view without zoom and turn\n555:- `game.view`: the view the game draws in now (the chosen one, with zoom and turn: read it, change it with setView)\n557:- `game.yaw = 0` †: its turn in degrees on top of the view (rotateView)\n691:- `rig.lastView` †: drawSmear projects the trail with the same view\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given\n----\n12: *    re-renders from another angle: E.VIEWS.iso, .threequarter, .topdown,\n13: *    .brawler, .side  (or build your own: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost)).\n548:class View {\n549:  /** new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per\n597:E.VIEWS = {\n2316:    this.view = this.baseView = this._view(this.o.view) || E.VIEWS.iso;\n2406:    const w = E.VIEWS[v];\n2407:    if (!w) warn('view:' + v, 'unknown view \"' + v + '\". Use one of: ' + Object.keys(E.VIEWS).join(', ') + ', or a new E.View(...)');\n2410:  /** switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn */\n8641:const VIEWS_BY_ID = id => E.VIEWS[id] || (warn('view:' + id, 'unknown view \"' + id + '\": ' + Object.keys(E.VIEWS).join(', ')), E.VIEWS.iso);\n10846:  _view(k) { const q = Math.round(k * 16) / 16; let v = this._views.get(q); if (!v) { v = new E.View('click', 'Click', 0, 20, q * 1.5, 1); this._views.set(q, v); } return v; }\n12402:    let v = this._views.get(key); if (!v) { if (this._views.size > 400) this._views.clear(); v = new E.View('mode7', 'Mode 7', yaw, this._pd, q, 1); this._views.set(key, v); }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"b6435ebf-cc1e-41ce-b547-ea9a60413d4d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:30.711Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"55:- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n219:## 3. Views (projections)\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n222:- `E.VIEW_ORDER: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side`: the order game.nextView() cycles through when a game doesn't set game.views ('overhead' is left out)\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n228:- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\n244:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n486:- `game.nextView(dir = 1)`: cycle through game.views (or every view): bind it to a key for players who like to switch\n488:- `game.onView(f)` †: call f(view) whenever the view changes (re-bake caches, move HUD)\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n494:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n515:- `game.baseView` †: the chosen view without zoom and turn\n555:- `game.view`: the view the game draws in now (the chosen one, with zoom and turn: read it, change it with setView)\n557:- `game.yaw = 0` †: its turn in degrees on top of the view (rotateView)\n691:- `rig.lastView` †: drawSmear projects the trail with the same view\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given\n----\n12: *    re-renders from another angle: E.VIEWS.iso, .threequarter, .topdown,\n13: *    .brawler, .side  (or build your own: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost)).\n548:class View {\n549:  /** new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per\n597:E.VIEWS = {\n2316:    this.view = this.baseView = this._view(this.o.view) || E.VIEWS.iso;\n2406:    const w = E.VIEWS[v];\n2407:    if (!w) warn('view:' + v, 'unknown view \"' + v + '\". Use one of: ' + Object.keys(E.VIEWS).join(', ') + ', or a new E.View(...)');\n2410:  /** switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn */\n8641:const VIEWS_BY_ID = id => E.VIEWS[id] || (warn('view:' + id, 'unknown view \"' + id + '\": ' + Object.keys(E.VIEWS).join(', ')), E.VIEWS.iso);\n10846:  _view(k) { const q = Math.round(k * 16) / 16; let v = this._views.get(q); if (!v) { v = new E.View('click', 'Click', 0, 20, q * 1.5, 1); this._views.set(q, v); } return v; }\n12402:    let v = this._views.get(key); if (!v) { if (this._views.size > 400) this._views.clear(); v = new E.View('mode7', 'Mode 7', yaw, this._pd, q, 1); this._views.set(key, v); }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GKFwhipoC47L1unRGW4iCi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
