{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018t4e1mHUJsuRCw7eGS5u1S","type":"tool_result","content":"30:game.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\n388:- `game.particles.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (the renderer calls it)\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n420:- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n422:- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\n440:- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n444:- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\n502:- `game.start(hooks)`: Start the loop. Either one scene: game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) }) or several: game.start({ scenes: { title: {...}, play: {...} }, scene: 'title' }) A scene is { enter(data), exit(), update(dt), draw(r), back(), pausable, view, views, input, res, expand, touch, camera } (all optional). start() with nothing resumes a stopped loop. A headless game, or one made with loop: false, runs only by advance().\n537:- `game.r`: the renderer handed to draw(r) (null when headless)\n603:- `new E.Path(points, o = {}) → path` †: new E.Path(points, { closed: false, smooth: null }): points [x, y, z] (z optional) or { x, y, z } (a side view's height is z); closed runs back to the first; smooth: 'catmull' curves through every point (Catmull-Rom); at(d), nearest(x, y, z), draw(r) below\n605:- `path.draw(r, color = '#ffe070')` †: draw it over the scene to see it (debugging): a line, and a dot at each of its points\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n1777:  groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0) { const pts = []; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const a = i / n * TAU; pts.push(this.w(x + Math.cos(a) * rad, y + Math.sin(a) * rad, z)); } return pts; }\n1779:  groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0) { px.polyDither(this.tgt, this.groundPts(x, y, rad, 18, z), color, alpha, this.ix, this.iy); }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"1a63b732-e64e-4840-a2fa-ce11c9be72fd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:05:33.174Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"30:game.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\n388:- `game.particles.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (the renderer calls it)\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n420:- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n422:- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\n440:- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n444:- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\n502:- `game.start(hooks)`: Start the loop. Either one scene: game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) }) or several: game.start({ scenes: { title: {...}, play: {...} }, scene: 'title' }) A scene is { enter(data), exit(), update(dt), draw(r), back(), pausable, view, views, input, res, expand, touch, camera } (all optional). start() with nothing resumes a stopped loop. A headless game, or one made with loop: false, runs only by advance().\n537:- `game.r`: the renderer handed to draw(r) (null when headless)\n603:- `new E.Path(points, o = {}) → path` †: new E.Path(points, { closed: false, smooth: null }): points [x, y, z] (z optional) or { x, y, z } (a side view's height is z); closed runs back to the first; smooth: 'catmull' curves through every point (Catmull-Rom); at(d), nearest(x, y, z), draw(r) below\n605:- `path.draw(r, color = '#ffe070')` †: draw it over the scene to see it (debugging): a line, and a dot at each of its points\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n1777:  groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0) { const pts = []; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const a = i / n * TAU; pts.push(this.w(x + Math.cos(a) * rad, y + Math.sin(a) * rad, z)); } return pts; }\n1779:  groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0) { px.polyDither(this.tgt, this.groundPts(x, y, rad, 18, z), color, alpha, this.ix, this.iy); }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018t4e1mHUJsuRCw7eGS5u1S","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","re