{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghriHcUoXSW3m4vUmGjN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now have what I need from the engine: the custom board view, ground polygons, input presets, the Dialog voice hook, and the save API. I've settled the scope and the architecture. Here is the decision, since the plan is far larger than one session can build well:\n\n- **Keep from the plan:** the hex tactical battles, the seasonal campaign loop (tidings, muster, march, aftermath), the Hour-Candle deadline, the AI for CPU realms and battles, story dialog with Animalese voices, the title and attract mode, dev-mode sliders, pad/keyboard/mouse input with PlayStation/Xbox glyphs, touch-only handling, an AI Hub round, and the About screen.\n- **Reduce, and say so in the final reply:** 16 castles instead of 25, 19 knights instead of 36, 8 species with 2 forms each instead of 30 with 3, 3 battle maps instead of 13, about 8 events instead of 40, and no hot-seat mode.\n- **Hub mode:** parallel (each player runs their own seeded skirmish and reports a score), not shared-world. That is simpler to make pass the harness.\n\nI'll start with the core module and the sim data, then test the simulations headless before building the scenes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14259,"cache_read_input_tokens":111589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14259},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"4b114ef7-ed30-475a-9a41-1f21a42d8d9c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:06:38.498Z","request_id":"req_011CghriHNbLxcQvkkvqk368"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghriHcUoXSW3m4vUmGjN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L8NV5PNUYe4pW4eKB16M3V","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050229/src/00-core.js","content":"// Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons. Core: the G namespace, the data registry, the random number generator, hex maths,\n// the live tunables. The core loop, written at the top as the plan asks:\n// each season, read the tidings, muster your castles (summon, bind, move, quest, equip), declare your marches, then fight\n// the battles they cause, until you can take Meridian before the Hour-Candle burns out.\n// Every file in src/ is concatenated inside one IIFE in name order, with `E` (the engine) and `G` (this game) in scope.\n\nG.TITLE = 'Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons';\nG.CORE_LOOP = 'Each season: read the tidings, muster your castles, declare your marches, fight what they cause.';\n\n// ---- data registry: G.def(kind, id, spec), G.get, G.all, G.ids, G.has (the data suite checks every reference) ----\nconst REG = Object.create(null);\nG.def = (kind, id, spec) => { (REG[kind] ||= new Map()).set(id, Object.assign({ id }, spec)); return REG[kind].get(id); };\nG.has = (kind, id) => !!(REG[kind] && REG[kind].has(id));\nG.get = (kind, id) => {\n  const v = REG[kind] && REG[kind].get(id);\n  if (!v) throw new Error('no ' + kind + ' \"' + id + '\"');\n  return v;\n};\nG.all = kind => (REG[kind] ? [...REG[kind].values()] : []);\nG.ids = kind => (REG[kind] ? [...REG[kind].keys()] : []);\n\n// ---- seeded random numbers (mulberry32). The state is plain JSON, so a saved battle replays exactly. ----\nG.Rng = class Rng {\n  constructor(seed = 1) { this.s = seed >>> 0; }\n  next() {\n    let t = (this.s = (this.s + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0);\n    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n  }\n  int(a, b) { return a + Math.floor(this.next() * (b - a + 1)); }       // inclusive\n  pick(list) { return list[Math.floor(this.next() * list.length)]; }\n  chance(p) { return this.next() < p; }\n  state() { return { s: this.s }; }\n  static from(st) { const r = new G.Rng(1); r.s = st.s >>> 0; return r; }\n};\n\n// ---- hex maths: pointy-top hexes in axial coordinates (q, r), screen y down. ----\nG.DIRS = [[1, 0], [1, -1], [0, -1], [-1, 0], [-1, 1], [0, 1]];          // E, NE, NW, W, SW, SE\nG.DIR_ANGLE = [0, -60, -120, 180, 120, 60];                             // screen degrees for the six directions\nG.key = (q, r) => q + ',' + r;\nG.parseKey = k => { const [q, r] = k.split(',').map(Number); return { q, r }; };\nG.hexDist = (a, b) => { const dq = a.q - b.q, dr = a.r - b.r; return (Math.abs(dq) + Math.abs(dr) + Math.abs(dq + dr)) / 2; };\nG.neighbours = (q, r) => G.DIRS.map(([dq, dr]) => ({ q: q + dq, r: r + dr }));\nG.offsetToAxial = (col, row) => ({ q: col - (row - (row & 1)) / 2, r: row });   // \"odd-r\": odd rows sit half a hex right\nG.hexWorld = (q, r, size) => ({ x: size * Math.sqrt(3) * (q + r / 2), y: size * 1.5 * r });\nG.hexRound = (fq, fr) => {\n  const fs = -fq - fr;\n  let q = Math.round(fq), r = Math.round(fr); const s = Math.round(fs);\n  const dq = Math.abs(q - fq), dr = Math.abs(r - fr), ds = Math.abs(s - fs);\n  if (dq > dr && dq > ds) q = -r - s; else if (dr > ds) r = -q - s;\n  return { q, r };\n};\nG.hexAtWorld = (x, y, size) => { const fr = y / (size * 1.5); return G.hexRound(x / (size * Math.sqrt(3)) - fr / 2, fr); };\nG.hexCorners = (x, y, size) => [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map(i => {\n  const a = (60 * i - 30) * Math.PI / 180;\n  return [x + size * Math.cos(a), y + size * Math.sin(a)];\n});\n// the direction (0..5) a screen vector points in, for keyboard and stick steering across a hex board\nG.dirFromVector = (mx, my) => {\n  const deg = Math.atan2(my, mx) * 180 / Math.PI;\n  let best = 0, bd = 999;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\n    let d = Math.abs(((deg - G.DIR_ANGLE[i]) % 360 + 540) % 360 - 180);\n    if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = i; }\n  }\n  return best;\n};\n\n// ---- live tunables: dev mode writes G.tune, the sims read it every time. Hub sessions always use the defaults. ----\nG.TUNE_DEFAULTS = {\n  battleDamage: 1,      // a multiplier on every hit\n  hitChance: 90,        // percent, before size, terrain and season\n  counterDamage: .6,    // a counter-attack's share of a normal hit\n  manaYield: 1,         // a multiplier on each castle's mana each season\n  summonCost: 1,        // a multiplier on what a monster costs to summon\n  questSeasons: 2,      // how many seasons a quest takes\n  candleSeasons: 12,    // how many seasons the Hour-Candle gives the player\n  bellLimit: 12,        // the bells a battle lasts before the defender holds\n  rivalAggression: 1,   // how eagerly the rival realms march (0 = never)\n  knightXp: 1           // a multiplier on the experience a knight earns\n};\nG.TUNE_RANGES = {\n  battleDamage: [.5, 2, .1], hitChance: [50, 100, 5], counterDamage: [0, 1, .1], manaYield: [.5, 2, .1],\n  summonCost: [.5, 2, .1], questSeasons: [1, 4, 1], candleSeasons: [6, 16, 1], bellLimit: [6, 16, 1],\n  rivalAggression: [0, 2, .1], knightXp: [0, 3, .5]\n};\nG.TUNE_LABELS = {\n  battleDamage: 'Battle damage', hitChance: 'Base hit chance', counterDamage: 'Counter-attack strength',\n  manaYield: 'Mana per castle', summonCost: 'Summon cost', questSeasons: 'Quest length (seasons)',\n  candleSeasons: 'Hour-Candle (seasons)', bellLimit: 'Bells per battle', rivalAggression: 'Rival aggression',\n  knightXp: 'Knight experience'\n};\nG.tune = Object.assign({}, G.TUNE_DEFAULTS);\nG.resetTune = () => Object.assign(G.tune, G.TUNE_DEFAULTS);\n\n// hash of a state object: a small FNV-1a over its JSON, for replays and tests\nG.hash = obj => {\n  const s = JSON.stringify(obj);\n  let h = 2166136261;\n  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) { h ^= s.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n  return (h >>> 0).toString(16);\n};\nG.clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14259,"cache_read_input_tokens":111589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14259},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"ebd221a2-356a-4df7-852d-612ebdfa06d3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:06:48.465Z","request_id":"req_011CghriHNbLxcQvkkvqk368","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01L8NV5PNUYe4pW4eKB16M3V":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050229/src/00-core.js","content":"// Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons. Core: the G namespace, the data registry, the random number generator, hex maths,\n// the live tunables. The core loop, written at the top as the plan asks:\n// each season, read the tidings, muster your castles (summon, bind, move, quest, equip), declare your marches, then fight\n// the battles they cause, until you can take Meridian before the Hour-Candle burns out.\n// Every file in src/ is concatenated inside one IIFE in name order, with `E` (the engine) and `G` (this game) in scope.\n\nG.TITLE = 'Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons';\nG.CORE_LOOP = 'Each season: read the tidings, muster your castles, declare your marches, fight what they cause.';\n\n// ---- data registry: G.def(kind, id, spec), G.get, G.all, G.ids, G.has (the data suite checks every reference) ----\nconst REG = Object.create(null);\nG.def = (kind, id, spec) => { (REG[kind] ||= new Map()).set(id, Object.assign({ id }, spec)); return REG[kind].get(id); };\nG.has = (kind, id) => !!(REG[kind] && REG[kind].has(id));\nG.get = (kind, id) => {\n  const v = REG[kind] && REG[kind].get(id);\n  if (!v) throw new Error('no ' + kind + ' \"' + id + '\"');\n  return v;\n};\nG.all = kind => (REG[kind] ? [...REG[kind].values()] : []);\nG.ids = kind => (REG[kind] ? [...REG[kind].keys()] : []);\n\n// ---- seeded random numbers (mulberry32). The state is plain JSON, so a saved battle replays exactly. ----\nG.Rng = class Rng {\n  constructor(seed = 1) { this.s = seed >>> 0; }\n  next() {\n    let t = (this.s = (this.s + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0);\n    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n  }\n  int(a, b) { return a + Math.floor(this.next() * (b - a + 1)); }       // inclusive\n  pick(list) { return list[Math.floor(this.next() * list.length)]; }\n  chance(p) { return this.next() < p; }\n  state() { return { s: this.s }; }\n  static from(st) { const r = new G.Rng(1); r.s = st.s >>> 0; return r; }\n};\n\n// ---- hex maths: pointy-top hexes in axial coordinates (q, r), screen y down. ----\nG.DIRS = [[1, 0], [1, -1], [0, -1], [-1, 0], [-1, 1], [0, 1]];          // E, NE, NW, W, SW, SE\nG.DIR_ANGLE = [0, -60, -120, 180, 120, 60];                             // screen degrees for the six directions\nG.key = (q, r) => q + ',' + r;\nG.parseKey = k => { const [q, r] = k.split(',').map(Number); return { q, r }; };\nG.hexDist = (a, b) => { const dq = a.q - b.q, dr = a.r - b.r; return (Math.abs(dq) + Math.abs(dr) + Math.abs(dq + dr)) / 2; };\nG.neighbours = (q, r) => G.DIRS.map(([dq, dr]) => ({ q: q + dq, r: r + dr }));\nG.offsetToAxial = (col, row) => ({ q: col - (row - (row & 1)) / 2, r: row });   // \"odd-r\": odd rows sit half a hex right\nG.hexWorld = (q, r, size) => ({ x: size * Math.sqrt(3) * (q + r / 2), y: size * 1.5 * r });\nG.hexRound = (fq, fr) => {\n  const fs = -fq - fr;\n  let q = Math.round(fq), r = Math.round(fr); const s = Math.round(fs);\n  const dq = Math.abs(q - fq), dr = Math.abs(r - fr), ds = Math.abs(s - fs);\n  if (dq > dr && dq > ds) q = -r - s; else if (dr > ds) r = -q - s;\n  return { q, r };\n};\nG.hexAtWorld = (x, y, size) => { const fr = y / (size * 1.5); return G.hexRound(x / (size * Math.sqrt(3)) - fr / 2, fr); };\nG.hexCorners = (x, y, size) => [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map(i => {\n  const a = (60 * i - 30) * Math.PI / 180;\n  return [x + size * Math.cos(a), y + size * Math.sin(a)];\n});\n// the direction (0..5) a screen vector points in, for keyboard and stick steering across a hex board\nG.dirFromVector = (mx, my) => {\n  const deg = Math.atan2(my, mx) * 180 / Math.PI;\n  let best = 0, bd = 999;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\n    let d = Math.abs(((deg - G.DIR_ANGLE[i]) % 360 + 540) % 360 - 180);\n    if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = i; }\n  }\n  return best;\n};\n\n// ---- live tunables: dev mode writes G.tune, the sims read it every time. Hub sessions always use the defaults. ----\nG.TUNE_DEFAULTS = {\n  battleDamage: 1,      // a multiplier on every hit\n  hitChance: 90,        // percent, before size, terrain and season\n  counterDamage: .6,    // a counter-attack's share of a normal hit\n  manaYield: 1,         // a multiplier on each castle's mana each season\n  summonCost: 1,        // a multiplier on what a monster costs to summon\n  questSeasons: 2,      // how many seasons a quest takes\n  candleSeasons: 12,    // how many seasons the Hour-Candle gives the player\n  bellLimit: 12,        // the bells a battle lasts before the defender holds\n  rivalAggression: 1,   // how eagerly the rival realms march (0 = never)\n  knightXp: 1           // a multiplier on the experience a knight earns\n};\nG.TUNE_RANGES = {\n  battleDamage: [.5, 2, .1], hitChance: [50, 100, 5], counterDamage: [0, 1, .1], manaYield: [.5, 2, .1],\n  summonCost: [.5, 2, .1], questSeasons: [1, 4, 1], candleSeasons: [6, 16, 1], bellLimit: [6, 16, 1],\n  rivalAggression: [0, 2, .1], knightXp: [0, 3, .5]\n};\nG.TUNE_LABELS = {\n  battleDamage: 'Battle damage', hitChance: 'Base hit chance', counterDamage: 'Counter-attack strength',\n  manaYield: 'Mana per castle', summonCost: 'Summon cost', questSeasons: 'Quest length (seasons)',\n  candleSeasons: 'Hour-Candle (seasons)', bellLimit: 'Bells per battle', rivalAggression: 'Rival aggression',\n  knightXp: 'Knight experience'\n};\nG.tune = Object.assign({}, G.TUNE_DEFAULTS);\nG.resetTune = () => Object.assign(G.tune, G.TUNE_DEFAULTS);\n\n// hash of a state object: a small FNV-1a over its JSON, for replays and tests\nG.hash = obj => {\n  const s = JSON.stringify(obj);\n  let h = 2166136261;\n  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) { h ^= s.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n  return (h >>> 0).toString(16);\n};\nG.clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L8NV5PNUYe4pW4eKB16M3V","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050229/src/00-core.js (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"3a913234-ce86-413e-a31f-9dabf77d12b6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:06:48.516Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050229/src/00-core.js","content":"// Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons. Core: the G namespace, the data registry, the random number generator, hex maths,\n// the live tunables. The core loop, written at the top as the plan asks:\n// each season, read the tidings, muster your castles (summon, bind, move, quest, equip), declare your marches, then fight\n// the battles they cause, until you can take Meridian before the Hour-Candle burns out.\n// Every file in src/ is concatenated inside one IIFE in name order, with `E` (the engine) and `G` (this game) in scope.\n\nG.TITLE = 'Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons';\nG.CORE_LOOP = 'Each season: read the tidings, muster your castles, declare your marches, fight what they cause.';\n\n// ---- data registry: G.def(kind, id, spec), G.get, G.all, G.ids, G.has (the data suite checks every reference) ----\nconst REG = Object.create(null);\nG.def = (kind, id, spec) => { (REG[kind] ||= new Map()).set(id, Object.assign({ id }, spec)); return REG[kind].get(id); };\nG.has = (kind, id) => !!(REG[kind] && REG[kind].has(id));\nG.get = (kind, id) => {\n  const v = REG[kind] && REG[kind].get(id);\n  if (!v) throw new Error('no ' + kind + ' \"' + id + '\"');\n  return v;\n};\nG.all = kind => (REG[kind] ? [...REG[kind].values()] : []);\nG.ids = kind => (REG[kind] ? [...REG[kind].keys()] : []);\n\n// ---- seeded random numbers (mulberry32). The state is plain JSON, so a saved battle replays exactly. ----\nG.Rng = class Rng {\n  constructor(seed = 1) { this.s = seed >>> 0; }\n  next() {\n    let t = (this.s = (this.s + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0);\n    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n  }\n  int(a, b) { return a + Math.floor(this.next() * (b - a + 1)); }       // inclusive\n  pick(list) { return list[Math.floor(this.next() * list.length)]; }\n  chance(p) { return this.next() < p; }\n  state() { return { s: this.s }; }\n  static from(st) { const r = new G.Rng(1); r.s = st.s >>> 0; return r; }\n};\n\n// ---- hex maths: pointy-top hexes in axial coordinates (q, r), screen y down. ----\nG.DIRS = [[1, 0], [1, -1], [0, -1], [-1, 0], [-1, 1], [0, 1]];          // E, NE, NW, W, SW, SE\nG.DIR_ANGLE = [0, -60, -120, 180, 120, 60];                             // screen degrees for the six directions\nG.key = (q, r) => q + ',' + r;\nG.parseKey = k => { const [q, r] = k.split(',').map(Number); return { q, r }; };\nG.hexDist = (a, b) => { const dq = a.q - b.q, dr = a.r - b.r; return (Math.abs(dq) + Math.abs(dr) + Math.abs(dq + dr)) / 2; };\nG.neighbours = (q, r) => G.DIRS.map(([dq, dr]) => ({ q: q + dq, r: r + dr }));\nG.offsetToAxial = (col, row) => ({ q: col - (row - (row & 1)) / 2, r: row });   // \"odd-r\": odd rows sit half a hex right\nG.hexWorld = (q, r, size) => ({ x: size * Math.sqrt(3) * (q + r / 2), y: size * 1.5 * r });\nG.hexRound = (fq, fr) => {\n  const fs = -fq - fr;\n  let q = Math.round(fq), r = Math.round(fr); const s = Math.round(fs);\n  const dq = Math.abs(q - fq), dr = Math.abs(r - fr), ds = Math.abs(s - fs);\n  if (dq > dr && dq > ds) q = -r - s; else if (dr > ds) r = -q - s;\n  return { q, r };\n};\nG.hexAtWorld = (x, y, size) => { const fr = y / (size * 1.5); return G.hexRound(x / (size * Math.sqrt(3)) - fr / 2, fr); };\nG.hexCorners = (x, y, size) => [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map(i => {\n  const a = (60 * i - 30) * Math.PI / 180;\n  return [x + size * Math.cos(a), y + size * Math.sin(a)];\n});\n// the direction (0..5) a screen vector points in, for keyboard and stick steering across a hex board\nG.dirFromVector = (mx, my) => {\n  const deg = Math.atan2(my, mx) * 180 / Math.PI;\n  let best = 0, bd = 999;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\n    let d = Math.abs(((deg - G.DIR_ANGLE[i]) % 360 + 540) % 360 - 180);\n    if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = i; }\n  }\n  return best;\n};\n\n// ---- live tunables: dev mode writes G.tune, the sims read it every time. Hub sessions always use the defaults. ----\nG.TUNE_DEFAULTS = {\n  battleDamage: 1,      // a multiplier on every hit\n  hitChance: 90,        // percent, before size, terrain and season\n  counterDamage: .6,    // a counter-attack's share of a normal hit\n  manaYield: 1,         // a multiplier on each castle's mana each season\n  summonCost: 1,        // a multiplier on what a monster costs to summon\n  questSeasons: 2,      // how many seasons a quest takes\n  candleSeasons: 12,    // how many seasons the Hour-Candle gives the player\n  bellLimit: 12,        // the bells a battle lasts before the defender holds\n  rivalAggression: 1,   // how eagerly the rival realms march (0 = never)\n  knightXp: 1           // a multiplier on the experience a knight earns\n};\nG.TUNE_RANGES = {\n  battleDamage: [.5, 2, .1], hitChance: [50, 100, 5], counterDamage: [0, 1, .1], manaYield: [.5, 2, .1],\n  summonCost: [.5, 2, .1], questSeasons: [1, 4, 1], candleSeasons: [6, 16, 1], bellLimit: [6, 16, 1],\n  rivalAggression: [0, 2, .1], knightXp: [0, 3, .5]\n};\nG.TUNE_LABELS = {\n  battleDamage: 'Battle damage', hitChance: 'Base hit chance', counterDamage: 'Counter-attack strength',\n  manaYield: 'Mana per castle', summonCost: 'Summon cost', questSeasons: 'Quest length (seasons)',\n  candleSeasons: 'Hour-Candle (seasons)', bellLimit: 'Bells per battle', rivalAggression: 'Rival aggression',\n  knightXp: 'Knight experience'\n};\nG.tune = Object.assign({}, G.TUNE_DEFAULTS);\nG.resetTune = () => Object.assign(G.tune, G.TUNE_DEFAULTS);\n\n// hash of a state object: a small FNV-1a over its JSON, for replays and tests\nG.hash = obj => {\n  const s = JSON.stringify(obj);\n  let h = 2166136261;\n  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) { h ^= s.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n  return (h >>> 0).toString(16);\n};\nG.clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01L8NV5PNUYe4pW4eKB16M3V","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
