Web Audio, AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0.',\n    'Art direction: the engine\\'s pixel style, with new rigs for knights and monsters, a painted continent, castles and banners in code.',\n    'Animation: the engine\\'s rigs and move set (E.move strikes, poses, walks), plus a bell-by-bell event queue for battles.',\n    'Audio: five songs, sound effects and Animalese babble voices, all synthesised in code. No audio files.',\n    'Online: AI Hub, parallel mode, 1 to 4 players: each plays a seeded skirmish and reports a score.',\n    'Testing: headless simulation tests (node tests/run.mjs), balance runs (node tools/simulate.mjs), and a hub harness run. Testing parameters allowed: the tools and the dev mode sliders.',\n    'Research: the engine\\'s API card and kits, the AI Hub README, the engine source for View, Dialog and saves. No outside research.',\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown.',\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium.',\n    'Usage: unknown. Cost is not estimated here.'] },\n  { heading: 'Testing feedback', lines: [\n    'Issues caught by testing: five. One crash (the Gray Knight\\'s size was a number, not a size class), two wrong expectations in my own tests, and two sim edge cases the tests now guard.',\n    'Critical or game-breaking: one. The crash would have stopped any battle the Gray Knight fights in.',\n    'Most helpful: the campaign playout, which plays every season to its end with a passive human and checks that it terminates on every seed.',\n    'Least helpful: the state-hash check, which only tests the hash function against itself.'] },\n  { heading: 'Engine feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: E.Humanoid and E.Blob with the E.move attack states, and the way rigs pose from plain state every step.',\n    'Stuck or guessed wrong: the pointer-to-ground mapping on a custom view, and which voice API the dialog takes per letter.',\n    'Most important thing built myself: the battle and campaign simulations, the hex board and its event queue, the list widget, and the pixel glyphs for PlayStation symbols.',\n    'Hardest part: fitting a tilted hex board to the screen with readable units.',\n    'Changed in the engine: nothing. The engine is used as shipped.',\n    'One thing to change: a per-letter voice callback on E.Dialog, so Animalese can be pitched per character without a pool.'] },\n  { heading: 'Prompt feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the clear list of what to build, and the file names, which left no doubt about the deliverables.',\n    'Confusing: the plan and the brief disagree on the names and the scope, and the plan asks for far more content than one session can build well.',\n    'Hardest: keeping the scope honest. Every feature in the brief is built; the plan\\'s content counts are not.',\n    'Would change: a short scope line that says which parts of the plan are required and which are optional.'] }\n];\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Hjy2x5RyqPQA4UqDS98CC1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
