{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghtgfFA7XEGSVXDBHe2i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`toGround` returns an array, so the hover code is correct. Next I'll bring the About text in line with what actually happened: nine issues were found, five of them game-breaking, and the engine feedback should mention only what I observed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2452,"cache_read_input_tokens":438679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2452},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"9c08aee4-044a-43de-ba9a-222dd92c9db1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:31:36.009Z","request_id":"req_011CghtgevK7JN9yuVVfyowP"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghtgfFA7XEGSVXDBHe2i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EkJ2kkXpA9udYCavCobBci","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/12-data-story.js'; s=open(p).read()\nstart=s.index(\"  { heading: 'Source Information', lines: [\")\nend=s.index(\"];\\n\", s.index(\"  { heading: 'Prompt feedback'\"))\nnew = \"\"\"  { heading: 'Source Information', lines: [\n    'Date: 2026-11-04 05:02:29',\n    'Source: Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin, 1998). Used for its tactics, its seasons of war and its tone.',\n    'Plan: PLAN.md, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort. Its architecture is followed; its content counts are scaled down.',\n    'Genre: turn-based strategy with a tactical hex battle layer. Perspective: an overhead map of the continent, a tilted hex board for battles, and dialogue scenes.',\n    'Tech: JavaScript on the my-3D2dge engine (v0.85.2, unchanged), canvas 2D, Web Audio, and the AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0.',\n    'Art direction: the engine\\\\'s pixel style. New rigs for knights and monsters, a painted continent, castles and banners drawn in code.',\n    'Animation: the engine\\\\'s rigs and move set (E.move strikes, poses and walks), and a bell-by-bell event queue for battles.',\n    'Audio: five songs, sound effects and Animalese babble voices, all synthesised in code. No audio files.',\n    'Online: AI Hub, parallel mode, 1 to 4 players. Each plays the same seeded skirmish and reports a score.',\n    'Testing: 241 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), balance runs, Playwright screenshots of every screen, and the AI Hub harness with 2 and 4 players.',\n    'Research: the engine\\\\'s API card, guide and kits, and the AI Hub README. No web search.',\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown.',\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium.',\n    'Usage: unknown. Cost is not estimated here.'] },\n  { heading: 'Testing feedback', lines: [\n    'Issues caught by testing and review: nine. Seven broke play; two were cosmetic.',\n    'Critical or game-breaking: five. A crash on any battle with the Gray Knight; a scene that could not reach the game; a resumed campaign with no castle selected; a campaign screen that could not draw; a battle card that could not draw.',\n    'Most helpful: the play suite, which drives real scenes with taps and time, and the screenshots, which showed draw errors that headless runs skip.',\n    'Least helpful: the state-hash check, which only tests the hash function against itself.'] },\n  { heading: 'Engine feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: E.Humanoid and E.Blob with the E.move attack states, and rigs that pose from plain state every step.',\n    'Stuck or guessed wrong: scenes do not receive their game, so I set it on each scene. A scene change takes a fade, so tests must wait for it. E.Dialog takes one voice, not a function, so I swap the voice each update.',\n    'Most important thing built myself: the battle and campaign simulations, the hex board and its event queue, the list widget, and the pixel glyphs for PlayStation symbols.',\n    'Hardest part: fitting a tilted hex board to the screen with readable units.',\n    'Changed in the engine: nothing. The engine is used as shipped.',\n    'One thing to change: a per-letter voice callback on E.Dialog, so Animalese can be pitched per character.'] },\n  { heading: 'Prompt feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the clear list of what to build, and the file names, which left no doubt about the deliverables.',\n    'Confusing: the plan and the brief disagree on the names and the scope, and the plan asks for far more content than one session can build well.',\n    'Hardest: keeping the scope honest. Every feature in the brief is built; the plan\\\\'s content counts are not.',\n    'Would change: a short scope line that says which parts of the plan are required and which are optional.'] }\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:start]+new+s[end:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\nnode -e \"1\" && node tools/build.mjs >/dev/null && node tests/run.mjs | tail -1 && node -e \"\nconst vm=require('vm'),fs=require('fs');const ctx={console};vm.createContext(ctx);\nvm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('engine/my-3d2dge.js','utf8'),ctx);vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('dist/game.js','utf8'),ctx);\nconsole.log('about sections:', ctx.My3D2dge.Brigantime.ABOUT.map(s=>s.heading+' ('+s.lines.length+')').join(' | '));\" 2>/dev/null","description":"Update About text with real test figures and rebuild"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2452,"cache_read_input_tokens":438679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2452},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"ece036e4-78e3-484e-8dda-019537a61d0c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:31:43.690Z","request_id":"req_011CghtgevK7JN9yuVVfyowP","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EkJ2kkXpA9udYCavCobBci":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050229 && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/12-data-story.js'; s=open(p).read()\nstart=s.index(\"  { heading: 'Source Information', lines: [\")\nend=s.index(\"];\\n\", s.index(\"  { heading: 'Prompt feedback'\"))\nnew = \"\"\"  { heading: 'Source Information', lines: [\n    'Date: 2026-11-04 05:02:29',\n    'Source: Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin, 1998). Used for its tactics, its seasons of war and its tone.',\n    'Plan: PLAN.md, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort. Its architecture is followed; its content counts are scaled down.',\n    'Genre: turn-based strategy with a tactical hex battle layer. Perspective: an overhead map of the continent, a tilted hex board for battles, and dialogue scenes.',\n    'Tech: JavaScript on the my-3D2dge engine (v0.85.2, unchanged), canvas 2D, Web Audio, and the AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0.',\n    'Art direction: the engine\\\\'s pixel style. New rigs for knights and monsters, a painted continent, castles and banners drawn in code.',\n    'Animation: the engine\\\\'s rigs and move set (E.move strikes, poses and walks), and a bell-by-bell event queue for battles.',\n    'Audio: five songs, sound effects and Animalese babble voices, all synthesised in code. No audio files.',\n    'Online: AI Hub, parallel mode, 1 to 4 players. Each plays the same seeded skirmish and reports a score.',\n    'Testing: 241 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), balance runs, Playwright screenshots of every screen, and the AI Hub harness with 2 and 4 players.',\n    'Research: the engine\\\\'s API card, guide and kits, and the AI Hub README. No web search.',\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown.',\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium.',\n    'Usage: unknown. Cost is not estimated here.'] },\n  { heading: 'Testing feedback', lines: [\n    'Issues caught by testing and review: nine. Seven broke play; two were cosmetic.',\n    'Critical or game-breaking: five. A crash on any battle with the Gray Knight; a scene that could not reach the game; a resumed campaign with no castle selected; a campaign screen that could not draw; a battle card that could not draw.',\n    'Most helpful: the play suite, which drives real scenes with taps and time, and the screenshots, which showed draw errors that headless runs skip.',\n    'Least helpful: the state-hash check, which only tests the hash function against itself.'] },\n  { heading: 'Engine feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: E.Humanoid and E.Blob with the E.move attack states, and rigs that pose from plain state every step.',\n    'Stuck or guessed wrong: scenes do not receive their game, so I set it on each scene. A scene change takes a fade, so tests must wait for it. E.Dialog takes one voice, not a function, so I swap the voice each update.',\n    'Most important thing built myself: the battle and campaign simulations, the hex board and its event queue, the list widget, and the pixel glyphs for PlayStation symbols.',\n    'Hardest part: fitting a tilted hex board to the screen with readable units.',\n    'Changed in the engine: nothing. The engine is used as shipped.',\n    'One thing to change: a per-letter voice callback on E.Dialog, so Animalese can be pitched per character.'] },\n  { heading: 'Prompt feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the clear list of what to build, and the file names, which left no doubt about the deliverables.',\n    'Confusing: the plan and the brief disagree on the names and the scope, and the plan asks for far more content than one session can build well.',\n    'Hardest: keeping the scope honest. Every feature in the brief is built; the plan\\\\'s content counts are not.',\n    'Would change: a short scope line that says which parts of the plan are required and which are optional.'] }\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:start]+new+s[end:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\nnode -e \"1\" && node tools/build.mjs >/dev/null && node tests/run.mjs | tail -1 && node -e \"\nconst vm=require('vm'),fs=require('fs');const ctx={console};vm.createContext(ctx);\nvm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('engine/my-3d2dge.js','utf8'),ctx);vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('dist/game.js','utf8'),ctx);\nconsole.log('about sections:', ctx.My3D2dge.Brigantime.ABOUT.map(s=>s.heading+' ('+s.lines.length+')').join(' | '));\" 2>/dev/null","description":"Update About text with real test figures and rebuild"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01EkJ2kkXpA9udYCavCobBci":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050229"}}}
