{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghtiLNQBDEKV52XQkYjR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The About sections now carry the corrected figures. Next is `exit-interview.json`, in the work folder beside the single HTML file. Every field in the required shape gets a real value, and I'll check that it parses."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3612,"cache_read_input_tokens":441131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3612},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"6e8eba96-5fa5-46e0-99ba-c8db6ca9a10a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:31:57.510Z","request_id":"req_011CghtiKuNzuK9aHP2buLPe"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghtiLNQBDEKV52XQkYjR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UJzPv8GjvhnufAntZuCKEh","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/exit-interview.json","content":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:29\",\n    \"source\": \"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin, PlayStation, 1998)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort; followed in its architecture, with its content counts scaled down)\",\n    \"genre\": \"Turn-based strategy with a tactical hex battle layer\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Overhead map of the continent; a tilted hex board for battles; side-on dialogue scenes\",\n    \"tech\": \"JavaScript on the my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (unchanged), canvas 2D, Web Audio, AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0; built to one HTML file by tools/build.mjs\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's pixel style: Humanoid and Blob rigs for knights and monsters, a painted continent, castles and banners drawn in code, PlayStation and Xbox button glyphs drawn in pixels\",\n    \"animation\": \"The engine's rigs and E.move attack states, poses and walks; a bell-by-bell event queue for battles (walks, strikes, hurts, deaths, bell banners)\",\n    \"audio\": \"Five songs in the engine's step-sequencer format, custom sound effects, and Animalese babble voices for dialogue, all synthesised in code; no audio files\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode, 1 to 4 players: each plays the same seeded skirmish and reports a score\",\n    \"testing\": \"241 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), balance runs (tools/simulate.mjs and tools/simulate-campaign.mjs), Playwright screenshots of every screen, and the AI Hub harness with 2 and 4 players under simulated latency and loss\",\n    \"research\": \"Read the engine's API card, AI guide, kits and source, and the AI Hub README. No web search.\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown (Playwright Chromium used for checks)\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"Nine issues: seven broke play (five of them game-breaking) and two were cosmetic. The game-breaking ones were a crash on any battle with the Gray Knight, scenes that could not reach the game object, a resumed campaign with no castle selected, a campaign screen that could not draw, and a battle card that could not draw. Two more came from my own wrong test expectations.\",\n    \"Five. A crash on any battle with the Gray Knight, a scene that could not reach the game, a resumed campaign with no selected castle, and two screens that threw while drawing (the campaign and the battle card). Each would have stopped a screen or a battle.\",\n    \"The play suite: it drives the real scenes with taps and time, and the screenshots, which showed draw errors that headless runs skip.\",\n    \"The state-hash check, which only tests the hash function against itself.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"E.Humanoid and E.Blob with the E.move attack states, and rigs that pose from plain state every step.\",\n    \"Scenes do not receive their game object, so I set it on each scene. A scene change takes a fade, so tests must wait for it before checking the new scene. E.Dialog takes one voice sound rather than a function, so I swap the voice each update to vary the babble.\",\n    \"The battle and campaign simulations, the hex board and its event queue, the list widget with mouse and pad focus, and the pixel glyphs for PlayStation symbols.\",\n    \"Fitting a tilted hex board to the screen with readable units, and keeping the unit cards and logs clear of the board.\",\n    \"Nothing. The engine is used as shipped; all game code is in src/ and the engine is unchanged.\",\n    \"A per-letter voice callback on E.Dialog, so Animalese can be pitched per character without a pool of sounds.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The clear list of what to build and the exact file names, which left no doubt about the deliverables.\",\n    \"The plan and the brief disagree on file names and scope, and the plan asks for far more content than one session can build well. The title also came from the plan's earlier draw, not one I made.\",\n    \"Keeping the scope honest. Every feature in the brief is built; the plan's content counts (25 castles, 36 knights, 30 species with 3 forms, 13 maps, 40 events) are not.\",\n    \"A short scope line that says which parts of the plan are required and which are optional, and a note on whether the title should be drawn again.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Four seasons, one clock running out\",\n    \"description\": \"A tactical strategy game in the spirit of Brigandine. Muster knights and monsters through four seasons, march on rival castles, and fight hex battles before the Hour-Candle burns out.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena\",\n    \"series\": \"Brigandine\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick or arrows move the cursor; A or Enter chooses; B or Escape backs out; Y or E ends your turns; the mouse hovers and clicks\",\n    \"tags\": [\"fantasy\", \"pixel art\", \"story\", \"versus\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3612,"cache_read_input_tokens":441131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3612},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"aac4f814-2eae-4e73-b69f-056dc299c90c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:32:06.107Z","request_id":"req_011CghtiKuNzuK9aHP2buLPe","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UJzPv8GjvhnufAntZuCKEh":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/exit-interview.json","content":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:29\",\n    \"source\": \"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin, PlayStation, 1998)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort; followed in its architecture, with its content counts scaled down)\",\n    \"genre\": \"Turn-based strategy with a tactical hex battle layer\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Overhead map of the continent; a tilted hex board for battles; side-on dialogue scenes\",\n    \"tech\": \"JavaScript on the my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (unchanged), canvas 2D, Web Audio, AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0; built to one HTML file by tools/build.mjs\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's pixel style: Humanoid and Blob rigs for knights and monsters, a painted continent, castles and banners drawn in code, PlayStation and Xbox button glyphs drawn in pixels\",\n    \"animation\": \"The engine's rigs and E.move attack states, poses and walks; a bell-by-bell event queue for battles (walks, strikes, hurts, deaths, bell banners)\",\n    \"audio\": \"Five songs in the engine's step-sequencer format, custom sound effects, and Animalese babble voices for dialogue, all synthesised in code; no audio files\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode, 1 to 4 players: each plays the same seeded skirmish and reports a score\",\n    \"testing\": \"241 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), balance runs (tools/simulate.mjs and tools/simulate-campaign.mjs), Playwright screenshots of every screen, and the AI Hub harness with 2 and 4 players under simulated latency and loss\",\n    \"research\": \"Read the engine's API card, AI guide, kits and source, and the AI Hub README. No web search.\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown (Playwright Chromium used for checks)\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"Nine issues: seven broke play (five of them game-breaking) and two were cosmetic. The game-breaking ones were a crash on any battle with the Gray Knight, scenes that could not reach the game object, a resumed campaign with no castle selected, a campaign screen that could not draw, and a battle card that could not draw. Two more came from my own wrong test expectations.\",\n    \"Five. A crash on any battle with the Gray Knight, a scene that could not reach the game, a resumed campaign with no selected castle, and two screens that threw while drawing (the campaign and the battle card). Each would have stopped a screen or a battle.\",\n    \"The play suite: it drives the real scenes with taps and time, and the screenshots, which showed draw errors that headless runs skip.\",\n    \"The state-hash check, which only tests the hash function against itself.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"E.Humanoid and E.Blob with the E.move attack states, and rigs that pose from plain state every step.\",\n    \"Scenes do not receive their game object, so I set it on each scene. A scene change takes a fade, so tests must wait for it before checking the new scene. E.Dialog takes one voice sound rather than a function, so I swap the voice each update to vary the babble.\",\n    \"The battle and campaign simulations, the hex board and its event queue, the list widget with mouse and pad focus, and the pixel glyphs for PlayStation symbols.\",\n    \"Fitting a tilted hex board to the screen with readable units, and keeping the unit cards and logs clear of the board.\",\n    \"Nothing. The engine is used as shipped; all game code is in src/ and the engine is unchanged.\",\n    \"A per-letter voice callback on E.Dialog, so Animalese can be pitched per character without a pool of sounds.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The clear list of what to build and the exact file names, which left no doubt about the deliverables.\",\n    \"The plan and the brief disagree on file names and scope, and the plan asks for far more content than one session can build well. The title also came from the plan's earlier draw, not one I made.\",\n    \"Keeping the scope honest. Every feature in the brief is built; the plan's content counts (25 castles, 36 knights, 30 species with 3 forms, 13 maps, 40 events) are not.\",\n    \"A short scope line that says which parts of the plan are required and which are optional, and a note on whether the title should be drawn again.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Four seasons, one clock running out\",\n    \"description\": \"A tactical strategy game in the spirit of Brigandine. Muster knights and monsters through four seasons, march on rival castles, and fight hex battles before the Hour-Candle burns out.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena\",\n    \"series\": \"Brigandine\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick or arrows move the cursor; A or Enter chooses; B or Escape backs out; Y or E ends your turns; the mouse hovers and clicks\",\n    \"tags\": [\"fantasy\", \"pixel art\", \"story\", \"versus\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\n"}}}
