{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghv3xd7vVisFuwD8ztL5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The mechanics are in and tested. Next I'll update the About text and the exit interview to match what's really built, and list plainly what isn't. Those two files are the only places where the claims are made."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":610499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":897},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"1a71f03f-4cab-4311-8b84-c8e5953ff46b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:49:26.979Z","request_id":"req_011Cghv3x8rViHAwHmgP9W5p"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghv3xd7vVisFuwD8ztL5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EUCDC7a75Unm8Q3XFpm7qY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/12-data-story.js'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"// the About and credits screen.\")\ns=s[:i]+'''// the About and credits screen. It carries the Source Information, the feedback lists the brief asks for, and what is not built.\nG.ABOUT = [\n  { heading: 'Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons', lines: [\n    'A tactical strategy game in the spirit of Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena. Four seasons, four realms, one clock running out. Built on my-3D2dge (v0.85.2) and AI Hub Session Protocol v1.',\n    'Made by Claude Haiku 5.5 (Anthropic). Every sound, voice, picture and song is drawn or synthesised in code.'] },\n  { heading: 'Source Information', lines: [\n    'Date: 2026-11-04 05:02:29',\n    'Source: Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin, 1998). Used for its tactics, its seasons of war and its tone.',\n    'Plan: PLAN.md, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort. Followed in its architecture and most of its content counts.',\n    'Genre: turn-based strategy with a tactical hex battle layer. Perspective: an overhead map of the continent, a tilted hex board for battles, and dialogue scenes.',\n    'Tech: JavaScript on the my-3D2dge engine (v0.85.2, unchanged), canvas 2D, Web Audio, and the AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0.',\n    'Art direction: the engine\\\\'s pixel style. Humanoid and Blob rigs for knights and monsters, a painted continent, castles and banners drawn in code.',\n    'Animation: the engine\\\\'s rigs and move set (E.move strikes, poses and walks), and a bell-by-bell event queue for battles.',\n    'Audio: five songs, sound effects and Animalese babble voices, all synthesised in code. No audio files.',\n    'Online: AI Hub, shared-world mode, 2 to 4 players. One battle; each player commands their own troop; the host copy runs the world.',\n    'Testing: 531 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), balance runs, Playwright screenshots of the screens, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode with 2 and 4 players, under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player.',\n    'Research: the engine\\\\'s API card, guide and kits, and the AI Hub README. No web search.',\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown.',\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium.',\n    'Usage: unknown. Cost is not estimated here.'] },\n  { heading: 'Content', lines: [\n    '25 castles and 36 knights on the continent, 30 monster species with three forms each, 33 items, 13 battle maps (the Clockwork Sanctum among them), 45 story events, 15 classes in five lines, and 7 endings.',\n    'Modes: campaign for 1 to 4 players on one device (hot-seat), skirmish against the CPU or hot-seat, shared-world AI Hub battle, attract mode, dev mode.'] },\n  { heading: 'Not built', lines: [\n    'Skills: 21 are built (the plan asks for 90). Unique ruler classes, the Stillness rule, the bespoke beast rigs of the plan (monsters use the engine\\\\'s Blob and Humanoid rigs), and the plan\\\\'s music by season.'] },\n  { heading: 'Testing feedback', lines: [\n    'Issues caught by testing and review: eleven across both rounds. Nine in the first round (seven broke play, two were cosmetic); two in the hub harness this round, where shared-world copies sent too little traffic.',\n    'Critical or game-breaking: five in the first round. A crash on any battle with the Gray Knight; a scene that could not reach the game; a resumed campaign with no castle selected; a campaign screen that could not draw; a battle card that could not draw.',\n    'Most helpful: the play suite, which drives real scenes with taps and time, and the screenshots, which showed draw errors that headless runs skip.',\n    'Least helpful: the state-hash check, which only tests the hash function against itself.'] },\n  { heading: 'Engine feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: E.Humanoid and E.Blob with the E.move attack states, and rigs that pose from plain state every step. E.Dialog choices worked as documented.',\n    'Stuck or guessed wrong: scenes do not receive their game object, so I set it on each scene. A scene change takes a fade, so tests must wait for it. E.Dialog takes one voice sound rather than a function, so I swap the voice each update.',\n    'Most important thing built myself: the battle and campaign simulations, the story triggers, the hex board and its event queue, the list widget with pad and mouse focus, the hub host protocol, and the pixel glyphs for PlayStation symbols.',\n    'Hardest part: fitting a tilted hex board to the screen with readable units, and making shared-world copies agree without a server.',\n    'Changed in the engine: nothing. The engine is used as shipped.',\n    'One thing to change: a per-letter voice callback on E.Dialog, so Animalese can be pitched per character.'] },\n  { heading: 'Prompt feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the clear list of what to build and the exact file names, which left no doubt about the deliverables.',\n    'Confusing: the plan and the brief disagree on file names and scope, and the plan asks for far more content than one session can build well. The title also came from the plan\\\\'s earlier draw, not one I made.',\n    'Hardest: keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built; the plan items listed under Not built are not.',\n    'Would change: a single scope line that says which parts of the plan are required and which are optional.'] }\n];\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs >/dev/null && node tests/run.mjs | tail -1","description":"Rewrite About text with current content and honest not-built list"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":610499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":897},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"633c050c-cc2e-4405-9549-fb04a2d52bb5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:49:35.268Z","request_id":"req_011Cghv3x8rViHAwHmgP9W5p","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EUCDC7a75Unm8Q3XFpm7qY":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050229 && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/12-data-story.js'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"// the About and credits screen.\")\ns=s[:i]+'''// the About and credits screen. It carries the Source Information, the feedback lists the brief asks for, and what is not built.\nG.ABOUT = [\n  { heading: 'Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons', lines: [\n    'A tactical strategy game in the spirit of Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena. Four seasons, four realms, one clock running out. Built on my-3D2dge (v0.85.2) and AI Hub Session Protocol v1.',\n    'Made by Claude Haiku 5.5 (Anthropic). Every sound, voice, picture and song is drawn or synthesised in code.'] },\n  { heading: 'Source Information', lines: [\n    'Date: 2026-11-04 05:02:29',\n    'Source: Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin, 1998). Used for its tactics, its seasons of war and its tone.',\n    'Plan: PLAN.md, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort. Followed in its architecture and most of its content counts.',\n    'Genre: turn-based strategy with a tactical hex battle layer. Perspective: an overhead map of the continent, a tilted hex board for battles, and dialogue scenes.',\n    'Tech: JavaScript on the my-3D2dge engine (v0.85.2, unchanged), canvas 2D, Web Audio, and the AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0.',\n    'Art direction: the engine\\\\'s pixel style. Humanoid and Blob rigs for knights and monsters, a painted continent, castles and banners drawn in code.',\n    'Animation: the engine\\\\'s rigs and move set (E.move strikes, poses and walks), and a bell-by-bell event queue for battles.',\n    'Audio: five songs, sound effects and Animalese babble voices, all synthesised in code. No audio files.',\n    'Online: AI Hub, shared-world mode, 2 to 4 players. One battle; each player commands their own troop; the host copy runs the world.',\n    'Testing: 531 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), balance runs, Playwright screenshots of the screens, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode with 2 and 4 players, under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player.',\n    'Research: the engine\\\\'s API card, guide and kits, and the AI Hub README. No web search.',\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown.',\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium.',\n    'Usage: unknown. Cost is not estimated here.'] },\n  { heading: 'Content', lines: [\n    '25 castles and 36 knights on the continent, 30 monster species with three forms each, 33 items, 13 battle maps (the Clockwork Sanctum among them), 45 story events, 15 classes in five lines, and 7 endings.',\n    'Modes: campaign for 1 to 4 players on one device (hot-seat), skirmish against the CPU or hot-seat, shared-world AI Hub battle, attract mode, dev mode.'] },\n  { heading: 'Not built', lines: [\n    'Skills: 21 are built (the plan asks for 90). Unique ruler classes, the Stillness rule, the bespoke beast rigs of the plan (monsters use the engine\\\\'s Blob and Humanoid rigs), and the plan\\\\'s music by season.'] },\n  { heading: 'Testing feedback', lines: [\n    'Issues caught by testing and review: eleven across both rounds. Nine in the first round (seven broke play, two were cosmetic); two in the hub harness this round, where shared-world copies sent too little traffic.',\n    'Critical or game-breaking: five in the first round. A crash on any battle with the Gray Knight; a scene that could not reach the game; a resumed campaign with no castle selected; a campaign screen that could not draw; a battle card that could not draw.',\n    'Most helpful: the play suite, which drives real scenes with taps and time, and the screenshots, which showed draw errors that headless runs skip.',\n    'Least helpful: the state-hash check, which only tests the hash function against itself.'] },\n  { heading: 'Engine feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: E.Humanoid and E.Blob with the E.move attack states, and rigs that pose from plain state every step. E.Dialog choices worked as documented.',\n    'Stuck or guessed wrong: scenes do not receive their game object, so I set it on each scene. A scene change takes a fade, so tests must wait for it. E.Dialog takes one voice sound rather than a function, so I swap the voice each update.',\n    'Most important thing built myself: the battle and campaign simulations, the story triggers, the hex board and its event queue, the list widget with pad and mouse focus, the hub host protocol, and the pixel glyphs for PlayStation symbols.',\n    'Hardest part: fitting a tilted hex board to the screen with readable units, and making shared-world copies agree without a server.',\n    'Changed in the engine: nothing. The engine is used as shipped.',\n    'One thing to change: a per-letter voice callback on E.Dialog, so Animalese can be pitched per character.'] },\n  { heading: 'Prompt feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the clear list of what to build and the exact file names, which left no doubt about the deliverables.',\n    'Confusing: the plan and the brief disagree on file names and scope, and the plan asks for far more content than one session can build well. The title also came from the plan\\\\'s earlier draw, not one I made.',\n    'Hardest: keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built; the plan items listed under Not built are not.',\n    'Would change: a single scope line that says which parts of the plan are required and which are optional.'] }\n];\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs >/dev/null && node tests/run.mjs | tail -1","description":"Rewrite About text with current content and honest not-built list"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01EUCDC7a75Unm8Q3XFpm7qY":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050229"}}}
