{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghv5SmKXznr4jpKLFcjV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MpZvxtG5NHmXEWDNfqnsqi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd = {\n \"sourceInformation\": {\n  \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:29\",\n  \"source\": \"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin, PlayStation, 1998)\",\n  \"plan\": \"PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort; followed in its architecture and most of its content counts; see Not built)\",\n  \"genre\": \"Turn-based strategy with a tactical hex battle layer\",\n  \"perspective\": \"Overhead map of the continent; a tilted hex board for battles; side-on dialogue scenes\",\n  \"tech\": \"JavaScript on the my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (unchanged), canvas 2D, Web Audio, AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0; built to one HTML file by tools/build.mjs\",\n  \"artDirection\": \"The engine's pixel style: Humanoid and Blob rigs for knights and monsters, a painted continent, castles and banners drawn in code, PlayStation and Xbox button glyphs drawn in pixels\",\n  \"animation\": \"The engine's rigs and E.move attack states, poses and walks; a bell-by-bell battle event queue (walks, strikes, hurts, deaths, bell banners, dial turns)\",\n  \"audio\": \"Five songs in the engine's step-sequencer format, custom sound effects, and Animalese babble voices for dialogue, all synthesised in code; no audio files\",\n  \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world mode, 2 to 4 players: one battle, each player commands their own troop, the host copy runs the world and broadcasts its state\",\n  \"testing\": \"531 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), balance runs (tools/simulate.mjs, tools/simulate-campaign.mjs), Playwright screenshots of the screens, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode with 2 and 4 players, under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player\",\n  \"research\": \"Read the engine's API card, AI guide, kits and source, and the AI Hub README. No web search.\",\n  \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown (Playwright Chromium used for checks)\",\n  \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n  \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n },\n \"testingFeedback\": [\n  \"Eleven issues across both rounds. Nine in the first round (seven broke play, two were cosmetic); two in the hub harness this round, where shared-world copies sent too little traffic.\",\n  \"Five critical in the first round: a crash on any battle with the Gray Knight, scenes that could not reach the game object, a resumed campaign with no selected castle, and two screens that threw while drawing (the campaign and the battle card). This round: none critical, but the hub round failed twice until the copies sent heartbeats and the host re-broadcast its state.\",\n  \"The play suite, which drives the real scenes with taps and time, and the screenshots, which showed draw errors that headless runs skip.\",\n  \"The state-hash check, which only tests the hash function against itself.\"\n ],\n \"engineFeedback\": [\n  \"E.Humanoid and E.Blob with the E.move attack states, rigs that pose from plain state every step, and E.Dialog choices, which worked as documented.\",\n  \"Scenes do not receive their game object, so I set it on each scene. A scene change takes a fade, so tests must wait for it. E.Dialog takes one voice sound rather than a function, so I swap the voice each update.\",\n  \"The battle and campaign simulations, the story triggers, the hex board and its event queue, the list widget with pad and mouse focus, the hub host protocol, and the pixel glyphs for PlayStation symbols.\",\n  \"Fitting a tilted hex board to the screen with readable units, and making shared-world copies agree without a server.\",\n  \"Nothing. The engine is used as shipped; all game code is in src/ and the engine is unchanged.\",\n  \"A per-letter voice callback on E.Dialog, so Animalese can be pitched per character without a pool of sounds.\"\n ],\n \"promptFeedback\": [\n  \"The clear list of what to build and the exact file names, which left no doubt about the deliverables.\",\n  \"The plan and the brief disagree on file names and scope, and the plan asks for far more content than one session can build well. The title also came from the plan's earlier draw, not one I made.\",\n  \"Keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built; the plan items listed under Not built are not (skills 21 of 90, unique ruler classes, Stillness, bespoke beast rigs, music by season).\",\n  \"A single scope line that says which parts of the plan are required and which are optional.\"\n ],\n \"aiHub\": {\n  \"name\": \"Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons\",\n  \"tagline\": \"Four seasons, one clock running out\",\n  \"description\": \"A tactical strategy game in the spirit of Brigandine. Muster knights and monsters through four seasons, march on rival castles, and fight hex battles before the Hour-Candle burns out, with a seasonal dials puzzle at the Clockwork Sanctum.\",\n  \"type\": \"Game\",\n  \"genre\": \"Strategy\",\n  \"source\": \"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena\",\n  \"series\": \"Brigandine\",\n  \"players\": \"1–4\",\n  \"controls\": \"Stick or arrows move the cursor; A or Enter chooses; B or Escape backs out; Y or E ends your turns; the mouse hovers and clicks\",\n  \"tags\": [\"fantasy\", \"pixel art\", \"story\", \"versus\", \"retro\"]\n }\n}\njson.dump(d, open('exit-interview.json','w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\nx = json.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\nprint('parses; testing', len(x['testingFeedback']), 'engine', len(x['engineFeedback']), 'prompt', len(x['promptFeedback']), 'empty', [k for k,v in x['sourceInformation'].items() if not v])\nEOF","description":"Regenerate exit-interview.json with current facts and validate it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3097,"cache_read_input_tokens":611396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3097},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"15dd75c2-7d9c-4beb-a8b0-e3067ca7512e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:49:55.133Z","request_id":"req_011Cghv5SPkmypsZNfYa18Jn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MpZvxtG5NHmXEWDNfqnsqi":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd = {\n \"sourceInformation\": {\n  \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:29\",\n  \"source\": \"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin, PlayStation, 1998)\",\n  \"plan\": \"PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort; followed in its architecture and most of its content counts; see Not built)\",\n  \"genre\": \"Turn-based strategy with a tactical hex battle layer\",\n  \"perspective\": \"Overhead map of the continent; a tilted hex board for battles; side-on dialogue scenes\",\n  \"tech\": \"JavaScript on the my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (unchanged), canvas 2D, Web Audio, AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0; built to one HTML file by tools/build.mjs\",\n  \"artDirection\": \"The engine's pixel style: Humanoid and Blob rigs for knights and monsters, a painted continent, castles and banners drawn in code, PlayStation and Xbox button glyphs drawn in pixels\",\n  \"animation\": \"The engine's rigs and E.move attack states, poses and walks; a bell-by-bell battle event queue (walks, strikes, hurts, deaths, bell banners, dial turns)\",\n  \"audio\": \"Five songs in the engine's step-sequencer format, custom sound