{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwpALgFXbAfQKcCBKN3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All five browser playthroughs pass: each campaign plays through the real screens to an ending with no errors, including a hot-seat run. Before I update the About text, I'll check the plan's remaining battle rules, capture and retreat, to see which are small enough to finish."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":749860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"c4771282-c3f6-46ae-a881-5016159afc34","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:12:33.384Z","request_id":"req_011Cghwp9pRZEAMSzzLrS6Qt"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwpALgFXbAfQKcCBKN3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JXuuPqFWM6QQNyhKmfdJq5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work && sed -n 594,612p PLAN.md | cut -c1-500","description":"Read the plan's rules for knights falling, retreat and capture"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":749860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"9c135a83-6f06-4dcd-bce9-e8babdd53684","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:12:34.054Z","request_id":"req_011Cghwp9pRZEAMSzzLrS6Qt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JXuuPqFWM6QQNyhKmfdJq5":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work && sed -n 594,612p PLAN.md | cut -c1-500","description":"Read the plan's rules for knights falling, retreat and capture"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JXuuPqFWM6QQNyhKmfdJq5","type":"tool_result","content":"### 5.9 Knights falling, retreat, capture and death\n- When a knight drops to 0 HP or retreats, its troop leaves the field. Each of its monsters still standing rolls for\n  capture if it is adjacent to an enemy knight or inside an enemy knight's Ward:\n  - chance = `captureBase` 25% + 25% if it was outside its own knight's Ward + 15% if below 30% HP, at most 75%;\n  - bosses and Hour elites (Pendulum Wyrm forms) never roll;\n  - a captured monster is taken by the nearest enemy knight (shown with a chain of light). After the battle it joins\n    the winner's reserve at the contested castle if its captor's side won, or the reserve of the captor's home castle\n    if it lost;\n  - every other monster retreats with its knight.\n- If a ruler falls or retreats, every knight on its side retreats at once and the side loses.\n- Monsters at 0 HP die and are gone for good (the Phoenix's Rebirth is the exception, §6.8). Knights at 0 HP are wounded\n  for the next season.\n\n### 5.10 Winning\n- A side loses the moment it has no knights on the field.\n- At the end of the last bell, the attacker wins if one of its knights stands on a Keep hex; otherwise the defender wins\n  and the attackers go home.\n- The Clockwork Sanctum and the hub skirmish have their own rules (§6.10, §11).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"f54140f1-a56e-4d61-816f-ce6bcf24e007","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:12:34.070Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 5.9 Knights falling, retreat, capture and death\n- When a knight drops to 0 HP or retreats, its troop leaves the field. Each of its monsters still standing rolls for\n  capture if it is adjacent to an enemy knight or inside an enemy knight's Ward:\n  - chance = `captureBase` 25% + 25% if it was outside its own knight's Ward + 15% if below 30% HP, at most 75%;\n  - bosses and Hour elites (Pendulum Wyrm forms) never roll;\n  - a captured monster is taken by the nearest enemy knight (shown with a chain of light). After the battle it joins\n    the winner's reserve at the contested castle if its captor's side won, or the reserve of the captor's home castle\n    if it lost;\n  - every other monster retreats with its knight.\n- If a ruler falls or retreats, every knight on its side retreats at once and the side loses.\n- Monsters at 0 HP die and are gone for good (the Phoenix's Rebirth is the exception, §6.8). Knights at 0 HP are wounded\n  for the next season.\n\n### 5.10 Winning\n- A side loses the moment it has no knights on the field.\n- At the end of the last bell, the attacker wins if one of its knights stands on a Keep hex; otherwise the defender wins\n  and the attackers go home.\n- The Clockwork Sanctum and the hub skirmish have their own rules (§6.10, §11).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JXuuPqFWM6QQNyhKmfdJq5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
