{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwwBHRCiwu5Dj7d1iUm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Battles still resolve, but the balance has moved: attackers take the Keep about half the time, and defenders no longer win by killing the commander. I'll note that as a known imbalance for the dev-mode sliders to tune, rather than hide it. Next I'll update the About text and the exit interview to the final facts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1136,"cache_read_input_tokens":761933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1136},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"71983855-232d-43a2-a911-1942eed58349","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:14:08.871Z","request_id":"req_011CghwwAs7YZfLWZokeCoqi"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwwBHRCiwu5Dj7d1iUm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y4pmbyUoNChhz9RxTYRwvN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/12-data-story.js'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    c=s.count(a); assert c==1,(c,a[:80]); s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"    'Testing: 531 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), balance runs, Playwright screenshots of the screens, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode with 2 and 4 players, under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player.',\",\n    \"    'Testing: 538 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), five browser playthroughs (node tests/run.mjs --browser), balance runs, Playwright screenshots of the screens, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode: 2 and 4 players, under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player.',\")\ni=s.index(\"  { heading: 'Content', lines: [\"); j=s.index(\"  { heading: 'Testing feedback'\")\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"  { heading: 'Content', lines: [\n    '25 castles and 36 knights on the continent. 30 monster species with three forms each, 23 classes in five lines plus eight unique ones, and 90 skills and spells from the plan\\\\'s table.',\n    '33 items, 13 battle maps (the Clockwork Sanctum among them), 46 story events with choices, rival lines between rulers, and 7 endings.',\n    'Battle rules: wards, forecast, capture of monsters, the commander\\\\'s retreat, Stillness on the campaign map, and the Season Dials of the Sanctum.',\n    'Modes: campaign for 1 to 4 players on one device (hot-seat), skirmish against the CPU or hot-seat, a shared-world AI Hub battle for 2 to 4 players, attract mode, dev mode.',\n    'Music: a theme for each season, the attacking and defending battle themes with a tension layer, the hourless and Sanctum themes, event and ending themes, and a sting when the season turns.'] },\n  { heading: 'Not built', lines: [\n    'Presentation details of the plan: the season wipe between seasons, troop figures on the continent map (banners stand in for them), the gallery tool, and the tutorial tips. Sound effects are a smaller set than the plan lists.',\n    'Balance: the first tuning is rough. Attackers take the Keep about half the time in planner battles. The dev sliders (battle damage, hit chance, counter-attack, knight experience) are the place to tune it.'] },\n\"\"\"+s[j:]\nrep(\"    'Issues caught by testing and review: eleven across both rounds. Nine in the first round (seven broke play, two were cosmetic); two in the hub harness this round, where shared-world copies sent too little traffic.',\",\n    \"    'Issues caught by testing and review: fourteen across all rounds. Nine in the first (seven broke play, two were cosmetic); two in the hub harness; and in the playthroughs, a campaign that never advanced its season, because a second muster press during a fade ended the wrong phase, and the rule that a battle could not restart after its rival lines.',\")\nrep(\"    'Keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built; the plan items listed under Not built are not.',\",\"    'Keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built, and the plan\\\\'s mechanics are built too; the items under Not built are presentation details and tuning.',\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs >/dev/null && node tests/run.mjs | tail -1","description":"Update About text with the final content and not-built list"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1136,"cache_read_input_tokens":761933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1136},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"8eef04e7-1c78-4d65-86b2-e4a5767c53a8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:14:14.112Z","request_id":"req_011CghwwAs7YZfLWZokeCoqi","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Y4pmbyUoNChhz9RxTYRwvN":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050229 && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/12-data-story.js'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    c=s.count(a); assert c==1,(c,a[:80]); s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"    'Testing: 531 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), balance runs, Playwright screenshots of the screens, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode with 2 and 4 players, under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player.',\",\n    \"    'Testing: 538 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), five browser playthroughs (node tests/run.mjs --browser), balance runs, Playwright screenshots of the screens, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode: 2 and 4 players, under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player.',\")\ni=s.index(\"  { heading: 'Content', lines: [\"); j=s.index(\"  { heading: 'Testing feedback'\")\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"  { heading: 'Content', lines: [\n    '25 castles and 36 knights on the continent. 30 monster species with three forms each, 23 classes in five lines plus eight unique ones, and 90 skills and spells from the plan\\\\'s table.',\n    '33 items, 13 battle maps (the Clockwork Sanctum among them), 46 story events with choices, rival lines between rulers, and 7 endings.',\n    'Battle rules: wards, forecast, capture of monsters, the commander\\\\'s retreat, Stillness on the campaign map, and the Season Dials of the Sanctum.',\n    'Modes: campaign for 1 to 4 players on one device (hot-seat), skirmish against the CPU or hot-seat, a shared-world AI Hub battle for 2 to 4 players, attract mode, dev mode.',\n    'Music: a theme for each season, the attacking and defending battle themes with a tension layer, the hourless and Sanctum themes, event and ending themes, and a sting when the season turns.'] },\n  { heading: 'Not built', lines: [\n    'Presentation details of the plan: the season wipe between seasons, troop figures on the continent map (banners stand in for them), the gallery tool, and the tutorial tips. Sound effects are a smaller set than the plan lists.',\n    'Balance: the first tuning is rough. Attackers take the Keep about half the time in planner battles. The dev sliders (battle damage, hit chance, counter-attack, knight experience) are the place to tune it.'] },\n\"\"\"+s[j:]\nrep(\"    'Issues caught by testing and review: eleven across both rounds. Nine in the first round (seven broke play, two were cosmetic); two in the hub harness this round, where shared-world copies sent too little traffic.',\",\n    \"    'Issues caught by testing and review: fourteen across all rounds. Nine in the first (seven broke play, two were cosmetic); two in the hub harness; and in the playthroughs, a campaign that never advanced its season, because a second muster press during a fade ended the wrong phase, and the rule that a battle could not restart after its rival lines.',\")\nrep(\"    'Keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built; the plan items listed under Not built are not.',\",\"    'Keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built, and the plan\\\\'s mechanics are built too; the items under Not built are presentation details and tuning.',\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs >/dev/null && node tests/run.mjs | tail -1","description":"Update About text with the final content and not-built list"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01Y4pmbyUoNChhz9RxTYRwvN":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910