{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwzD5tfrFp2BQiS3E31","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E7JqAqsf8bNoZW9FHD5dY9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\nsi=d['sourceInformation']\nsi['plan']=\"PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort; followed in its architecture, its mechanics and most of its content counts; presentation details and tuning are not built)\"\nsi['tech']=\"JavaScript on the my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (unchanged), canvas 2D, Web Audio, AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0; built to one HTML file by tools/build.mjs\"\nsi['artDirection']=\"The engine's pixel style: Humanoid and Blob rigs, bespoke beast rigs (quadruped, drake, avian, serpent), a painted continent, castles and banners drawn in code, PlayStation and Xbox button glyphs drawn in pixels\"\nsi['animation']=\"The engine's rigs and E.move attack states, poses and walks; beast rigs with walk, wing and sway motion; a bell-by-bell battle event queue (walks, strikes, hurts, deaths, captures, dial turns)\"\nsi['audio']=\"Season themes, battle themes (attacking and defending, with a tension layer), the hourless and Sanctum themes, event and ending themes, stings, and Animalese babble voices, all synthesised in code; no audio files\"\nsi['testing']=\"538 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), five browser playthroughs through the real scenes (node tests/run.mjs --browser), balance runs, Playwright screenshots, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode with 2 and 4 players under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player\"\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"Fourteen issues across all rounds. Nine in the first round (seven broke play, two were cosmetic); two in the hub harness; and in the playthroughs, a campaign that never advanced its season (a second muster press during a fade ended the wrong phase), and a battle that could not restart after its rival lines.\",\n \"Five critical in the first round: a crash on any battle with the Gray Knight, scenes that could not reach the game object, a resumed campaign with no selected castle, and two screens that threw while drawing. Two of this round's are game-breaking for a campaign: the season that never advanced, and the battle that did not resume after the rival lines.\",\n \"The play suite, which drives the real scenes with taps and time, and the browser playthroughs, which run whole campaigns through the screens; the screenshots showed draw errors that headless runs skip.\",\n \"The state-hash check, which only tests the hash function against itself.\"]\nd['engineFeedback'][2]=\"The battle and campaign simulations, the story triggers, the skill engine with areas and statuses, the hex board and its event queue, the list widget with pad and mouse focus, the hub host protocol, the beast rigs, and the pixel glyphs for PlayStation symbols.\"\nd['promptFeedback'][2]=\"Keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built, and the plan's mechanics are built too; presentation details (season wipe, troop figures on the map, the gallery tool, tutorial tips) and balance tuning are not finished.\"\nd['aiHub']['description']=\"A tactical strategy game in the spirit of Brigandine. Muster knights and monsters through four seasons, march on rival castles, and fight hex battles with 90 skills, before the Hour-Candle burns out; the Clockwork Sanctum's dials guard the final gate.\"\njson.dump(d, open('exit-interview.json','w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\nx=json.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\nprint('parses; testing', len(x['testingFeedback']), 'engine', len(x['engineFeedback']), 'prompt', len(x['promptFeedback']), 'empty', [k for k,v in x['sourceInformation'].items() if not v], [k for k,v in x['aiHub'].items() if v in ('',[])])\nEOF","description":"Update the exit interview JSON with the final facts and validate it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1757,"cache_read_input_tokens":766310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1757},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"87b7146b-6488-4ff1-9639-def8f17fc6ae","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:14:52.240Z","request_id":"req_011CghwzCk4cF8dqbmX34YDU","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01E7JqAqsf8bNoZW9FHD5dY9":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\nsi=d['sourceInformation']\nsi['plan']=\"PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort; followed in its architecture, its mechanics and most of its content counts; presentation details and tuning are not built)\"\nsi['tech']=\"JavaScript on the my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (unchanged), canvas 2D, Web Audio, AI Hub client session.js v1.4.0; built to one HTML file by tools/build.mjs\"\nsi['artDirection']=\"The engine's pixel style: Humanoid and Blob rigs, bespoke beast rigs (quadruped, drake, avian, serpent), a painted continent, castles and banners drawn in code, PlayStation and Xbox button glyphs drawn in pixels\"\nsi['animation']=\"The engine's rigs and E.move attack states, poses and walks; beast rigs with walk, wing and sway motion; a bell-by-bell battle event queue (walks, strikes, hurts, deaths, captures, dial turns)\"\nsi['audio']=\"Season themes, battle themes (attacking and defending, with a tension layer), the hourless and Sanctum themes, event and ending themes, stings, and Animalese babble voices, all synthesised in code; no audio files\"\nsi['testing']=\"538 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), five browser playthroughs through the real scenes (node tests/run.mjs --browser), balance runs, Playwright screenshots, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode with 2 and 4 players under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player\"\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"Fourteen issues across all rounds. Nine in the first round (seven broke play, two were cosmetic); two in the hub harness; and in the playthroughs, a campaign that never advanced its season (a second muster press during a fade ended the wrong phase), and a battle that could not restart after its rival lines.\",\n \"Five critical in the first round: a crash on any battle with the Gray Knight, scenes that could not reach the game object, a resumed campaign with no selected castle, and two screens that threw while drawing. Two of this round's are game-breaking for a campaign: the season that never advanced, and the battle that did not resume after the rival lines.\",\n \"The play suite, which drives the real scenes with taps and time, and the browser playthroughs, which run whole campaigns through the screens; the screenshots showed draw errors that headless runs skip.\",\n \"The state-hash check, which only tests the hash function against itself.\"]\nd['engineFeedback'][2]=\"The battle and campaign simulations, the story triggers, the skill engine with areas and statuses, the hex board and its event queue, the list widget with pad and mouse focus, the hub host protocol, the beast rigs, and the pixel glyphs for PlayStation symbols.\"\nd['promptFeedback'][2]=\"Keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built, and the plan's mechanics are built too; presentation details (season wipe, troop figures on the map, the gallery tool, tutorial tips) and balance tuning are not finished.\"\nd['aiHub']['description']=\"A tactical strategy game in the spirit of Brigandine. Muster knights and monsters through four seasons, march on rival castles, and fight hex battles with 90 skills, before the Hour-Candle burns out; the Clockwork Sanctum's dials guard the final gate.\"\njson.dump(d, open('exit-interview.json','w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\nx=json.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\nprint('parses; testing', len(x['testingFeedback']), 'engine', len(x['engineFeedback']), 'prompt', len(x['promptFeedback']), 'empty', [k for k,v in x['sourceInformation'].items() if not v], [k for k,v in x['aiHub'].items() if v in ('',[])])\nEOF","description":"Update the exit interview JSON with the final facts and validate it"}}}
