{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghydWBCPgdovgDtCFoiC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LC1f9WaqJwFbifT2WN6oVL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/exit-interview.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']=\"546 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), five browser playthroughs through the real scenes (node tests/run.mjs --browser), balance runs against the plan's targets (not all met; see Not built), Playwright screenshots, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode with 2 and 4 players under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player\"\nd['sourceInformation']['audio']=\"Season themes, battle themes (attacking and defending, with a tension layer), the hourless and Sanctum themes, event and ending themes, the plan's named sound effects (UI, battle, spells by season, statuses, outcomes, creatures, world and timers), and per-letter Animalese voices driven by each speaker's profile; all synthesised in code, no audio files\"\nd['promptFeedback'][2]=\"Keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built, and the plan's mechanics, sound-effect list and content counts are built too. The plan's balance targets are not met on measurement, which I report as such; the dev sliders are the way to tune them.\"\nd['testingFeedback'][0]=\"Fourteen issues across all rounds. Nine in the first round (seven broke play, two cosmetic); two in the hub harness; and three in the playthroughs and review: a campaign that never advanced its season, a battle that could not restart after its rival lines, and a balance rule (the Keep won mid-move) that the plan puts at the end of the last bell. This round, a stray comma broke the build once, and the autoplay tests exposed that rulers were falling in defence.\"\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nx=json.load(open(p)); print('parses', len(x['testingFeedback']), len(x['engineFeedback']), len(x['promptFeedback']), [k for k,v in x['sourceInformation'].items() if not v])\nEOF\ncd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work && ls | cut -c1-120","description":"Update and validate the exit interview; list the work folder"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1016,"cache_read_input_tokens":863793,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1016},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"b19b0e96-a5c2-46c5-a824-32a16729e7d7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:36:21.681Z","request_id":"req_011CghydVfhRLHYcQa3bGRoW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LC1f9WaqJwFbifT2WN6oVL":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work/exit-interview.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']=\"546 headless checks (node tests/run.mjs), five browser playthroughs through the real scenes (node tests/run.mjs --browser), balance runs against the plan's targets (not all met; see Not built), Playwright screenshots, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode with 2 and 4 players under latency and loss, with a host leaving, and with a host that has no player\"\nd['sourceInformation']['audio']=\"Season themes, battle themes (attacking and defending, with a tension layer), the hourless and Sanctum themes, event and ending themes, the plan's named sound effects (UI, battle, spells by season, statuses, outcomes, creatures, world and timers), and per-letter Animalese voices driven by each speaker's profile; all synthesised in code, no audio files\"\nd['promptFeedback'][2]=\"Keeping the scope honest. Every feature the brief names is built, and the plan's mechanics, sound-effect list and content counts are built too. The plan's balance targets are not met on measurement, which I report as such; the dev sliders are the way to tune them.\"\nd['testingFeedback'][0]=\"Fourteen issues across all rounds. Nine in the first round (seven broke play, two cosmetic); two in the hub harness; and three in the playthroughs and review: a campaign that never advanced its season, a battle that could not restart after its rival lines, and a balance rule (the Keep won mid-move) that the plan puts at the end of the last bell. This round, a stray comma broke the build once, and the autoplay tests exposed that rulers were falling in defence.\"\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nx=json.load(open(p)); print('parses', len(x['testingFeedback']), len(x['engineFeedback']), len(x['promptFeedback']), [k for k,v in x['sourceInformation'].items() if not v])\nEOF\ncd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work && ls | cut -c1-120","description":"Update and validate the exit interview; list the work folder"}}}
