{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghysBzhvQ2m4qV63iszt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Doubling and tripling player mana gave identical results, which means mana isn't the binding constraint. The likely cap is my one-summon-per-castle-per-season rule. I'll check what the plan says about summoning before I change anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1255,"cache_read_input_tokens":883511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1255},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"6507c69f-f794-485a-83f3-fec9080c486c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:39:27.366Z","request_id":"req_011CghysBWBvFXJptZB1zqTs"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghysBzhvQ2m4qV63iszt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0187jN8RTXyp5YvAU3MgeQsT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work && sed -n 282,331p PLAN.md | cut -c1-420","description":"Read the plan's rules for seasons, mana, summoning and binding"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1255,"cache_read_input_tokens":883511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1255},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"e74e274c-6ccc-40c0-ba10-90ad1dc37ea9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:39:28.127Z","request_id":"req_011CghysBWBvFXJptZB1zqTs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0187jN8RTXyp5YvAU3MgeQsT":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050229__x7910ab/work && sed -n 282,331p PLAN.md | cut -c1-420","description":"Read the plan's rules for seasons, mana, summoning and binding"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0187jN8RTXyp5YvAU3MgeQsT","type":"tool_result","content":"### 4.2 Seasons outside battle\n- **Income:** castles whose region's season is the current season yield +25% (`tune.seasonYield`).\n- **Wintering:** in Winter, every non-Winter monster's upkeep is +25% (`tune.winterUpkeep`).\n- **AI:** a realm in its own season has ×1.2 aggression.\n- **Presentation:** the map recolours and its weather, music and Tidings banner change (\"WINTER. Hoarfast's knights grow\n  bold.\").\n- Effects inside battles are in §5.11.\n\n### 4.3 The three phases of a season\n1. **Tidings** (automatic, one card at a time; confirm advances, hold to skip all):\n   1. the season card (the Wheel turns to the new season, with that season's sting);\n   2. the candle burns, if it is lit;\n   3. recovery: wounds tick down, every unit at a castle returns to full HP and MP, and last season's Stilled castle\n      wakes;\n   4. Stillness picks a new castle (§4.16);\n   5. quests return (§4.9);\n   6. income minus upkeep, per realm (the report shows the player's own);\n   7. story events (at most 3 scenes a Tidings; the rest wait for the next one, §6.12);\n   8. the AI realms run their Muster instantly (their results are visible on the map).\n2. **Muster** (each human realm in seat order; a privacy card between humans, §10.8): the actions in §4.5–4.11, in any\n   order, as often as their limits allow. End with □ (Space on a keyboard) held for 0.6 s, or Commands → End Muster, then a confirm.\n3. **March:** each human declares attacks (§4.12), then each AI realm declares (hidden until resolution), then the\n   battles resolve (§4.13). After the last aftermath, the season ends and the next Tidings begins.\n\n### 4.4 Castles\nEach castle has `{ id, name, region (season or hour or neutral), tier, mana, circle: [species], site, map,\ntreasury, pos: [x, y], roads: [ids] }` from data (§6.2) and `{ owner, knights: [ids], reserve: [monster ids], stilled,\ntreasuryTaken }` in state. At most 6 knights can be stationed in one castle. Every player sees every castle's knights\nand troops (the source hides nothing, and neither does this game).\n\n### 4.5 Mana\n- **Yields per season:** capital 40, inner castle 25, flank castle 20, cross-quarter (brigand) castle 30, Hour satellite\n  30, Meridian 60. All are scaled by `tune.manaIncome`.\n- **Starting mana:** 120 for each season-realm and 300 for the Dominion. Brigands have no economy.\n- **Each Tidings:** mana += income − Σ upkeep. If the result is below 0, monsters desert one at a time, the lowest power\n  per point of upkeep first, until mana ≥ 0 (each loss is reported).\n\n### 4.6 Summon\nAt an owned castle that is not Stilled, pick a tier-1 species from its circle (entries marked with a season can be\nsummoned only in that season). Pay `cost × tune.summonCost`. The monster appears in the castle's reserve at level\n`max(1, floor(average level of the realm's knights / 2))`. Each castle allows at most 3 summons per season. Upkeep is\ncharged from the next Tidings.\n\n### 4.7 Bind (Organize)\nMove monsters between a castle's reserve and the knights stationed there. A troop holds at most 6 monsters, and their\nbond costs (rank, §6.8) may not add up to more than the knight's **Bond** (class base + floor(level / 4), plus items).\nEach knight also has a **formation** (Vanguard, Shield or Column, §5.2). A reserve monster can be **dismissed** (it is\ngone; ask first).\n\n### 4.8 Move","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b593beda-ab71-4ff5-909e-67cc1a56f914","uuid":"c5a01827-49b6-4a46-80d1-2c05cb497ac6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:39:28.147Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 4.2 Seasons outside battle\n- **Income:** castles whose region's season is the current season yield +25% (`tune.seasonYield`).\n- **Wintering:** in Winter, every non-Winter monster's upkeep is +25% (`tune.winterUpkeep`).\n- **AI:** a realm in its own season has ×1.2 aggression.\n- **Presentation:** the map recolours and its weather, music and Tidings banner change (\"WINTER. Hoarfast's knights grow\n  bold.\").\n- Effects inside battles are in §5.11.\n\n### 4.3 The three phases of a season\n1. **Tidings** (automatic, one card at a time; confirm advances, hold to skip all):\n   1. the season card (the Wheel turns to the new season, with that season's sting);\n   2. the candle burns, if it is lit;\n   3. recovery: wounds tick down, every unit at a castle returns to full HP and MP, and last season's Stilled castle\n      wakes;\n   4. Stillness picks a new castle (§4.16);\n   5. quests return (§4.9);\n   6. income minus upkeep, per realm (the report shows the player's own);\n   7. story events (at most 3 scenes a Tidings; the rest wait for the next one, §6.12);\n   8. the AI realms run their Muster instantly (their results are visible on the map).\n2. **Muster** (each human realm in seat order; a privacy card between humans, §10.8): the actions in §4.5–4.11, in any\n   order, as often as their limits allow. End with □ (Space on a keyboard) held for 0.6 s, or Commands → End Muster, then a confirm.\n3. **March:** each human declares attacks (§4.12), then each AI realm declares (hidden until resolution), then the\n   battles resolve (§4.13). After the last aftermath, the season ends and the next Tidings begins.\n\n### 4.4 Castles\nEach castle has `{ id, name, region (season or hour or neutral), tier, mana, circle: [species], site, map,\ntreasury, pos: [x, y], roads: [ids] }` from data (§6.2) and `{ owner, knights: [ids], reserve: [monster ids], stilled,\ntreasuryTaken }` in state. At most 6 knights can be stationed in one castle. Every player sees every castle's knights\nand troops (the source hides nothing, and neither does this game).\n\n### 4.5 Mana\n- **Yields per season:** capital 40, inner castle 25, flank castle 20, cross-quarter (brigand) castle 30, Hour satellite\n  30, Meridian 60. All are scaled by `tune.manaIncome`.\n- **Starting mana:** 120 for each season-realm and 300 for the Dominion. Brigands have no economy.\n- **Each Tidings:** mana += income − Σ upkeep. If the result is below 0, monsters desert one at a time, the lowest power\n  per point of upkeep first, until mana ≥ 0 (each loss is reported).\n\n### 4.6 Summon\nAt an owned castle that is not Stilled, pick a tier-1 species from its circle (entries marked with a season can be\nsummoned only in that season). Pay `cost × tune.summonCost`. The monster appears in the castle's reserve at level\n`max(1, floor(average level of the realm's knights / 2))`. Each castle allows at most 3 summons per season. Upkeep is\ncharged from the next Tidings.\n\n### 4.7 Bind (Organize)\nMove monsters between a castle's reserve and the knights stationed there. A troop holds at most 6 monsters, and their\nbond costs (rank, §6.8) may not add up to more than the knight's **Bond** (class base + floor(level / 4), plus items).\nEach knight also has a **formation** (Vanguard, Shield or Column, §5.2). A reserve monster can be **dismissed** (it is\ngone; ask first).\n\n### 4.8 Move","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0187jN8RTXyp5YvAU3MgeQsT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
